    "text": "\u003c@U0B4UMFK7C3\u003e Yes, OLake requires access to Docker images to fetch and run the connector images.\nYou currently have 2 options:\n1. Use OLake with internet access so it can pull the required images from Docker Hub.\n2. Use OLake in an offline setup:\n• \u003chttps://olake.io/docs/install/olake-ui/offline-environments-aws/?utm_source=chatgpt.com|OLake UI for Offline environments (AWS)\u003e\n• \u003chttps://olake.io/docs/install/olake-ui/offline-environments-generic/?utm_source=chatgpt.com|OLake UI for Offline environments (Generic)\u003e\nYour current logs indicate that OLake is unable to reach Docker Hub, which is why the image tag fetching is failing.",
